1. She has a dog that wakes her up early in the morning. (Verbatim: "my dog's like ohio ohio ohio the sun has risen walk me i'm like please no no no")
2. She is a self-described "overthinking kind of warrior." (Verbatim: "i'm a kind of uh overthinking kind of warrior")
3. She is not well-versed in horror films and considers herself a "certified wimp." (Verbatim: "i'm not well versed in horror films i'm i'm quite a wimp i'm a certified wimp")
4. She finds it difficult to stay up late due to time zone differences. (Verbatim: "time zones time zones are my greatest enemy like my goodness")
5. She has difficulty with late-night streams and often needs to nap afterward. (Verbatim: "i couldn't okay i couldn't so yesterday yesterday i had to go out all day um yeah so i went on like a two-hour walk")
6. She recently debuted in a new form and is excited about it. (Verbatim: "i'm very excited to have debuted i'm very excited to um be in this form")
7. She has a close relationship with her "mama elia," who is likely a family member or close companion. (Verbatim: "i went to see mama elia got back had collab no time for nap no time for nap")
8. She enjoys watching movies, particularly older films like Halloween (1978). (Verbatim: "we were watching um halloween halloween i think i think that's the one")
9. She is not a fan of slasher films and was shocked by the protagonist's poor survival choices. (Verbatim: "i was so shocked i was like okay i give you i give you um praise for your good kill")
10. She has a habit of checking her phone while resting, often on the sofa. (Verbatim: "i was on the sofa and mama elia's just like caught up on my phone like i'm so tired") [end of text]



1. She once bought a massive bag of pasta to last her an entire year while studying at university. (Verbatim: "so I bought a mahoosive a mahoosive bag of pasta okay just picture like the biggest bag of pasta you could buy")
2. She stored the pasta in a cupboard to the left of the sink. (Verbatim: "I put it in the cupboard not under the sink but to the left of under the sink")
3. The entire bag of pasta was eaten by rats, leaving only a hole in the plastic and droppings behind. (Verbatim: "the whole thing every bit of pasta was gone like the entire bag the whole thing every bit of my giant bulk pasta pack was gone there was a big big hole the plastic remained there was a big hole at the bottom which had been numbed open")
4. She discovered the rats had an escape route through a gap at the back of the cupboard. (Verbatim: "there was also there was like a gap at the back of the cupboard which i'm pretty certain was their escape route")
5. She cried after discovering her pasta stash had been destroyed by rats. (Verbatim: "and then i cried")
6. She recruited a campus cat to live with her after the rat infestation. (Verbatim: "then i recruited the campus cat to stay with me")
7. She finds it creepy to hear rats in the walls. (Verbatim: "it's really creepy when you can hear them in the walls have you guys ever heard rats and moles it's scary they're like")
8. She has had bats in her living space before. (Verbatim: "i've had bats before inside but bats are difficult because they fly and and yeah like yeah")
9. She is deeply emotional about the delay of her debut date, nearly crying when it was postponed. (Verbatim: "if we had to move it again i was gonna cry um actually no i did almost cry because it was originally gonna be")
10. She expressed a strong desire to be free in her VTuber form and to finally reveal her debut date. (Verbatim: "i just wanted to be in this form and to be free") [end of text]



1. She is working on re-releasing her "Letters of Comfort" series in a consistent format. (Verbatim: "in regards to my letters of comfort um that will be coming back that will be coming back and um and i will be re-releasing the ones that are there in this form so that it's consistent")
2. She stopped her "Letters of Comfort" series because she thought she was nearing her debut, but it kept getting delayed. (Verbatim: "basically i stopped it because i was getting well i thought i was getting near debut um and and then i just kept getting pushed and moved and and yeah um basically that's what happened")
3. She has a strong desire to be good at everything except sports. (Verbatim: "i want to be good at everything every every everything all the skills maybe not sport i'm okay with not being good at sport")
4. She struggles with motivation to tidy up her space. (Verbatim: "i wish i was more motivated to tidy it's just not in my nature")
5. She has a personal goal to improve herself despite having flaws. (Verbatim: "i still have many improvements that yeah there's still like how messy i've been recently and scattered and i just yeah yeah i have flaws but thank you for accepting me with my flaws")
6. She values being worthy of her role as a VTuber and strives to meet expectations. (Verbatim: "i'll do my best to be to be worthy of being a she yeah")
7. She is open to experimenting with different formats for her content, including ASMR. (Verbatim: "i could just have an asmr version um i don't know yeah you guys yeah like maybe i think just having two versions for people that like asmr and people that don't")
8. She has experience creating a custom game with two weak, non-threatening Pokémon-like creatures. (Verbatim: "there's two like Pokemon-like creatures in the game that I programmed one is a swing and one is a moth")
9. She used voice actors Elp and Viterra in her debut, who provided voice work for key characters. (Verbatim: "So it was Elp Hi They did so good making the sounds They gave me such a selection Like of sounds to use")
10. She has basic piano skills, though she considers them poor. (Verbatim: "i technically have well yeah i technically have i do have piano just really bad at it") [end of text]



1. She has struggled with swimming despite multiple attempts over many years. (Verbatim: "i've had swimming lessons it's just not happening okay i've i've i've tried it's and i know i'm stubborn but but so many so many years of swimming lessons i just gotta admit defeat at some point")
2. She values kindness as a core personal principle, which she has upheld since school. (Verbatim: "i've believed in that rule since since like school and stuff and there were a lot of times where i doubted that rule like when people wouldn't stop bullying me at school even though i did my best to be kind")
3. She has experienced bullying in school despite consistently trying to be kind. (Verbatim: "when people wouldn't stop bullying me at school even though i did my best to be kind")
4. She is self-aware of her lack of confidence and is actively working to improve it. (Verbatim: "i'm very aware of and maybe a bit too aware of but do you know i'm working hard okay")
5. She is nervous about singing, which was her biggest concern during her debut. (Verbatim: "the thing i was most nervous about at debut was definitely the singing")
6. She admires other VTubers' singing abilities and feels motivated by them. (Verbatim: "they're inspiring though like like yeah comparison is bad i'm using and i mean it more in a inspirational kind of kind of way")
7. She wants to expand her vocal range beyond choir songs. (Verbatim: "i want to be able to do other songs that aren't choir songs i want my ability to be more ranged")
8. She has attempted to play guitar but abandoned it due to lack of skill. (Verbatim: "i wanted originally to do the backing and acoustic guitar but i'm not good enough for guitar to to do that so i didn't")
9. She enjoys eating Special K bars, particularly the juicy red berry flavor. (Verbatim: "i really like special k bars but they're too yummy and i end up eating the whole box normally")
10. She has a strong emotional connection to her debut, describing it as a culmination of many struggles. (Verbatim: "many sleepless nights many many struggles but i wouldn't change a thing i would not change a thing nope no not a thing") [end of text]



1. She created a custom online survey as part of her debut content. (Verbatim: "i made it a form and i did my best to make it look like paper and and and on the clipboard")
2. She values creativity in her debut presentation and wanted to avoid traditional slides. (Verbatim: "i didn't actually incorporate too much information actually in the game like there's a bit about fears there's the karaoke part of a debut but not actually like the slides")
3. She has a preference for using technology to create visually appealing content rather than technical work. (Verbatim: "i just want to use tech to make pretty things")
4. She completed a master's degree and has since been in a period of rest. (Verbatim: "after my master's was like yeah i need to just chill i've been chilling for a while guys")
5. She is currently focused on content creation and community engagement after her debut. (Verbatim: "now we've reached debut and i'll be posting lots of content so the number may go up")
6. She has a goal of reaching 50,000 subscribers for "socks", 100,000 for "thighs", and 200,000 for "feet" as part of her subscriber milestones. (Verbatim: "goals 50k sub for socks 100k for thighs and 200k for feet")
7. She is not interested in technical roles involving Kubernetes or similar systems. (Verbatim: "if you have experience with kubernetes clusters we have an opening i do not wish to do any")
8. She appreciates being reminded of her responsibilities by others, such as her friend Ellie Bro. (Verbatim: "i put this girl on my schedule and i get a message from ellie bro being like yo you sure you're okay paying disco elysium")
9. She values the support and presence of her community, often expressing affection toward them. (Verbatim: "i just want to hug you guys that's all that's all")
10. She has a playful, self-aware attitude toward her own content and production choices. (Verbatim: "i made it so much harder for myself") [end of text]



1. She is recovering from her debut weekend, which was extremely energy-draining. (Verbatim: "although i'm still recovering from from debut weekend because my goodness that took a lot of energy out of me")
2. She has a strong emotional reaction to being praised, often holding back tears due to past experiences. (Verbatim: "i've been holding myself back here and i've been a yeah yeah yeah i was always told off for crying actually")
3. She was raised to believe crying was not allowed, which makes her anxious about showing emotion. (Verbatim: "i was raised um being told crying was not allowed it isn't great but yeah yeah so i guess i get scared if i cry a little")
4. She has a family background in the military, with multiple generations from her father's side having served. (Verbatim: "in my family um pretty much all the generations from like my dad's side from papa elia's side have like been in the army")
5. Her generation on her father's side has not pursued military service, which she finds notable. (Verbatim: "but my generation none of us have ah well there's always the guys so that that i that's not an excuse that's not an excuse")
6. She finds military training physically demanding and impressive, especially observing a roommate who participated in OTC. (Verbatim: "it looked like it's so she was like having to carry all this heavy stuff and go so far i'd like just do so much exercise and outdoors i don't know how she did it")
7. She is not naturally inclined to rehearse and prefers improvising, though she prepared extensively for her debut. (Verbatim: "i'm not one to rehearse i'm more of a let's wing it do it once uh but i prepped tons")
8. She worked on her debut content up until the last minute, contributing to its rushed nature. (Verbatim: "i was working on stuff up until the end so yeah oh gosh um yeah so if any parts don't seem polished that is that that is why")
9. She values natural performance and avoids scripted delivery, aiming for authenticity in her streams. (Verbatim: "i didn't want it to sound scripted in any way um so to really get across that like natural acting vibe")
10. She uses a Stream Deck with multi-action macros to automate scene changes, audio adjustments, and model movements during streams. (Verbatim: "you can set up um if you have a stream deck um one of the best features of the stream deck is you can set up this thing called multi-action") [end of text]



1. She has difficulty recognizing faces, leading to awkward social situations. (Verbatim: "they're like it's nothing personal i'm just blind to faces go man go")
2. She once confused two people with similar outfits and voices at a work farewell event, causing embarrassment. (Verbatim: "i had to go to like um a work leaving do once and and like there were two girls that went and they wore they wore very similar outfits and their voices are kind of similar and and i mixed them up and and they got very very very upset")
3. She experiences strong emotional reactions to past awkward moments and often replays them in her mind. (Verbatim: "i went home and cringed looking back at my memories lying in bed like i could sleep or i could think back to cringe moments yay good brain um")
4. She is aware of her tendency to get overly emotional during streams and tries to hold herself back. (Verbatim: "i told you like all stream that i'm trying to hold myself back on being emotional but but y'all")
5. Her debut stream lasted 58 minutes. (Verbatim: "58 minutes, okay, so that would be the last one and then anyone anything else after that will be post")
6. She values emotional connection with her audience and sees her debut as a gift to them. (Verbatim: "this debut is my gift to you you're not supposed to give back you punks you're supposed to look after yourself")
7. She has a habit of forgetting messages or notifications due to being overwhelmed. (Verbatim: "Wait i didn't see the message. I keep missing it you're too fast.")
8. She is self-conscious about appearing silly or villainous in her stream reactions. (Verbatim: "oh gosh i do look like a villain there oh dear and dear and dear um")
