1. She has a strong emotional connection to her community and feels deeply supported by them. (Verbatim: "you've really helped me through some tough times never failing to make me smile")
2. She struggled with feelings of not fitting in during much of her life. (Verbatim: "I'm just a weird British girl I'm just a strange girl that never really got to fit in most of their life")
3. She grew up in a financially modest environment, often relying on inexpensive food. (Verbatim: "I'm still living on beans but that's because beans are yummy")
4. She values kindness and believes everyone deserves it, regardless of their circumstances. (Verbatim: "everyone deserves kindness never say you do yeah you deserve to be kind to yourself")
5. She has a deep appreciation for the emotional support she receives from her fans. (Verbatim: "watching you has helped me through some confusing and uncertain times")
6. She has a dream of creating a welcoming space where people feel they belong. (Verbatim: "I just wanted to make somewhere where people could be happy and feel welcome even if no matter what you're like")
7. She identifies as British and embraces that identity. (Verbatim: "I'm just a weird British girl I'm just a strange girl that never really got to fit in")
8. She feels unworthy of the kindness shown to her by her community. (Verbatim: "I don't know if I deserve all the kindness that you guys give me")
9. She has a childhood memory of being told her dream of making people happy was silly. (Verbatim: "the teacher told you you were silly for wanting to just make people happy")
10. She views her VTuber debut as a gift to her community, not a personal reward. (Verbatim: "this debut is my present to you and I want to keep bringing in your presents") [end of text]



1. She feels she has been a "mess" recently and has struggled with doing many things well. (Verbatim: "I feel like I've been such a mess recently and that I've been trying to do so much that I've been failing in many many areas of things that I normally do.")
2. She fears she has disappointed her audience. (Verbatim: "I was really scared and I really thought I disappointed you guys.")
3. She believes people are generally nice, even if they act poorly due to misdirected emotions. (Verbatim: "I feel like people are always a lot of people are nice in their own way and I think a lot of difficulties in life come through people not understanding the intentions behind people.")
4. She values kindness and believes it is essential, especially for those who have been mistreated. (Verbatim: "I feel like kindness is important right.")
5. She has difficulty staying awake during long drives, which are required for her work. (Verbatim: "I have a hard time staying awake for long drives which I have to do for work.")
6. She streams every day. (Verbatim: "I do stream every day I'll be streaming every day.")
7. She feels she doesn't deserve the love and support she receives. (Verbatim: "I don't want to make ya angry wait... I don't have anything... I don't know I just worried I've I know I say I'm a mess but I'm your mess.")
8. She sees herself as imperfect, cringe, and not edgy. (Verbatim: "I might be a mess and I might be cringe and I might not be cool and I'm definitely definitely definitely not edgy in the slightest.")
9. She views herself as a reflection of others' light rather than a source of it. (Verbatim: "I'm just the moon reflecting I'm just the moon reflecting I'm just the moon reflecting.")
10. She encourages others to be kind to themselves and to embrace being "dumb dumbs" together. (Verbatim: "So let's be dumb dumbs together okay yeah nice big already deserve everything we give.") [end of text]



1. She is an adult despite appearing younger than her actual age. (Verbatim: "but no i really am i'm an adult for real for real")
2. She has a younger-looking face that has led to people mistaking her for being younger than she is. (Verbatim: "i've always been told that i look younger and that it'll pay off when i'm older")
3. She has flat feet, which causes her knees to go inward. (Verbatim: "my knees do go inwards because i have flat feet")
4. She has small feet, specifically UK size 4, and can sometimes buy children's shoes. (Verbatim: "i have uk size 4 which means which isn't too small but it means it's small enough that like i can buy children's shoes sometimes")
5. She finds ice skating extremely difficult due to her flat feet and inward knees. (Verbatim: "ice skating extremely difficult i'll be honest um don't ever take the ice skating i will cling to the wall like there's no tomorrow")
6. She was denied access to child-sized skating aids (like penguin skates) because she is considered too old. (Verbatim: "they won't give them to me because apparently i'm too old and and it's for children only")
7. She dislikes wearing velcro shoes at public facilities like bowling alleys, as they make her feel like a child. (Verbatim: "i got heckin velcro like excuse me i could tie my laces punk")
8. Her VTuber model was originally inspired by a specific bag she wanted as her oshi mark. (Verbatim: "my entire design was originally based on this bag so like when i was trying to think what form i'd like um i wanted this as my oshi mark")
9. She requested a smaller chest size for her model but was given a larger one, which she attributes to "booba life chose me." (Verbatim: "i did ask for a smaller chest um um i did ask for a smaller chest i didn't honestly i didn't choose the booba life the booba life chose me")
10. She has expressive facial animations including a physics-based tongue and pout that cannot be toggled. (Verbatim: "the tongue has physics it's very strange yeah i'm literally poking my tongue out it's not a toggle") [end of text]



1. She is in her late teens or early twenties, having been in her final year of school (Year 11). (Verbatim: "when i was in the eldest year i had people in like the younger the younger years so like i was year 11")
2. She has experienced being mistaken for a younger student due to her appearance. (Verbatim: "i'd have the little tiny year eights come up to me and pat me on the head and be like wow what a cute little year seven")
3. She finds it awkward when younger people pat her head despite being older than them. (Verbatim: "am year 11 please leave me alone")
4. She has a provisional driving license that expired in January. (Verbatim: "that expired in like january yeah january")
5. She passed her driving theory test but never completed driving lessons due to financial issues and lockdown. (Verbatim: "i did pass my theory test and i was gonna get driving lessons um but then two things happened um the money for the thriving lessons kapoofed and and then the whole lockdown thing happened")
6. She has not driven a car and is unfamiliar with automatic transmission systems. (Verbatim: "i've never been in an automatic car like i'm trying to picture a car without the clutch and without the stickier stick i can't picture one")
7. She is hesitant to carry her passport due to its perceived importance. (Verbatim: "i don't want to carry around my passport what it what if that feels it feels too important to carry around you know")
8. She is aware of age restrictions on certain products like energy drinks, lottery tickets, and sharp objects. (Verbatim: "there's like age restrictions not just on alcohol but on things like um energy drinks and and lottery ticket things and whatnot")
9. She has been unable to claim small winnings from a lottery due to being denied access because of her age. (Verbatim: "mama elia might do like a lottery thing and maybe she wins a tiny little amount like a tenner okay she's like 10 buckaroos and she'll be like elia go to the shop claim my monies for me and i'll be like okie dokie go to shop gets refused gets refused my tenor because they're like id please")
10. She finds the concept of automatic cars confusing and is still trying to understand their controls. (Verbatim: "i'm just not used to seeing spin is it so you can drift like do donuts sleepy what the heck is s n r i'm scrolling through this wiki how article okay it doesn't tell me what the s is") [end of text]



1. She values empathy and respect for all things, even inanimate objects. (Verbatim: "I don't want to insult a chair either... it's not just applicable to cars.")
2. She believes beauty is subjective and respects differing aesthetic opinions. (Verbatim: "Beauty is subjective... it's only ew to me.")
3. She experienced social anxiety around expressing opinions in school. (Verbatim: "I felt like this a lot in school... having an opinion would just be a reason for people to potentially make fun of you.")
4. She grew up listening to both pop and rock/punk music from her parents. (Verbatim: "I grew up with having to listen to music from both mama elia and papa elia who have very very very different tastes.")
5. She enjoys a wide variety of music and has no issue with different genres. (Verbatim: "I've never had any issue with both... they both you know make me like.")
6. She has a strong opinion about the Halloween movie, finding it funny and frustrating. (Verbatim: "I did give a very very strong opinion on the halloween movie that's because you guys make me feel comfortable.")
7. She values core values and ethics over shared interests in relationships. (Verbatim: "If your inner principles and values align you will get along incredibly well.")
8. She has close friends from college with very different interests but shared core values. (Verbatim: "I have those friends from college that like very different things... we have the same core values.")
9. She enjoys pineapple on pizza and believes those who say they don’t are lying. (Verbatim: "yeah we all like pineapple on pizza anyone who says they don't is lying okay")
10. She is involved in creating a multi-game interactive project with three different engines. (Verbatim: "the problem with making the game accessible is it's actually three games... three different styles") [end of text]



1. She created a simple side-scrolling game using RPG Maker. (Verbatim: "so basically with the side scroller super simple because there's nothing in the game but walking to the left or right")
2. She manually added every image in her game individually. (Verbatim: "like each each picture is individually added")
3. She spent significant time creating detailed pixel art, including subtle textures like wool. (Verbatim: "i spent i spent time making this very subtle wool")
4. She values appreciation from her audience and wants to find multiple ways to show gratitude. (Verbatim: "i want to find more ways i want to make everybody here feel appreciated")
5. She has a strong emotional connection to her audience, stating they bring her joy even when lurking. (Verbatim: "you guys bring a lot of joy even if you're lurking in something like those the numbers add up")
6. She enjoys cute aesthetics and is unapologetic about liking them. (Verbatim: "i just wanna like the the things that make me smile and and just the pink the pink the cute pink and the cute purples")
7. She grew up with brothers who mocked anything she found cute. (Verbatim: "i obviously grew up with brothers you know where anything cute would be like what's the word um laughed at")
8. She faced social judgment in university for wearing cute, floaty skirts while others wore casual clothing. (Verbatim: "i remember wearing my my my cute floaty skirt and then overhearing a girl talking about me like laughing at me with the other girls saying like making fun of me for putting in effort")
9. She believes some people never grow out of immature behavior, even in adulthood. (Verbatim: "you realize um you realize as you get older some people some people never grow out of that")
10. She has a small, compact PC case that she chose for its aesthetic appeal despite technical limitations. (Verbatim: "i just really wanted this case because it was cute i'm sorry and slash not sorry") [end of text]



1. She has a dog who sniffs flies and then knocks them around. (Verbatim: "i have a dog and and she just sniffs them up her nose and then snorts them back out and then like sniffs them up again snorts them back out and then just like knocks it about and i'm like girl stop")
2. She created and released a custom cursor for her VTuber debut. (Verbatim: "i got a little ellie cursor that i was gonna release um for debut i'm still gonna release it but then but then there are also some um wonderful cursors commissioned of of the whole of videre that are also wonderful")
