1. She is British. (Verbatim: "I am I am british hi yes um yeah it was very confusing because like the tofairy would give some people like i don't know one pound some some kids would get a two pound coin and and some kids would get a full-on five pound note and i was getting 50ps if i was lucky and i was like well no you know what i was always told about this about this i was always told that um it's because i wasn't i needed to be i needed to be gooder i needed more good like yeah it was like you're being treated unfairly by santa because you're not a good enough child and i was like i was like oh oh okay i will try and be gooder i will i will try um still didn't explain why santa used the same wrapping paper as my parents though i'm just saying like i feel like yeah but why is it why is it the same though why why is it all the same handwriting as you like i have many i had so many logistical questions as well like like how did how did the sleigh work i need to i i was i i wanted to know the science behind it and and nobody could answer it and and it was very very confusing so yeah and they were like don't ask questions and i'm like but questions curiosity is good for the mind")
2. She had a conflicted childhood understanding of Christmas magic due to inconsistencies in gift-giving. (Verbatim: "i remember being confused why santa was a bit unfair with gift giving depending on the kid like and the tooth fairy why was my tooth fairy always on holiday and the few times my tooth fairy wasn't on holiday um she didn't give much")
3. She believes Santa and the Tooth Fairy operate under unfair or inconsistent rules, leading to skepticism. (Verbatim: "i was like oh oh okay i will try and be gooder i will i will try um still didn't explain why santa used the same wrapping paper as my parents though i'm just saying like i feel like yeah but why is it why is it the same though why why is it all the same handwriting as you like i have many i had so many logistical questions as well like like how did how did the sleigh work i need to i i was i i wanted to know the science behind it and and nobody could answer it and and it was very very confusing so yeah")
4. She has a strong interest in the mechanics and logic behind mythical traditions like Santa and the Tooth Fairy. (Verbatim: "i was i i wanted to know the science behind it and and nobody could answer it and and it was very very confusing so yeah")
5. She values curiosity and believes questioning is beneficial for the mind. (Verbatim: "but questions curiosity is good for the mind")
6. Her mother loves Christmas and enjoys watching Christmas movies year-round. (Verbatim: "mama elia loves christmas though like yeah i know i know my presents um may not have been as expensive as like other kids um but it didn't mean they didn't care mama elia loves christmas and um she she liked to watch christmas movies like a lot")
7. Her mother watches a 24/7 Christmas movie channel on TV. (Verbatim: "there's a channel on tv there's a channel on tv that just plays christmas movies 24 7 like like there's an entire channel just dedicated to playing christmas movies non-stop mama elia loved that channel like like it was just always on and i'd be like it's like july can we not like yeah")
8. Her father has a negative view of Christmas, seeing it as overly commercialized and believes it should focus only on family. (Verbatim: "papa elia believes that christmas has become a commercialized abomination and it should only be about the love of family with no need for presents um and decor and people have forgotten the true meaning of it um so they have very different views on christmas um so yeah it's just quite difficult um")
9. She has a detailed annual Christmas spreadsheet for gift planning. (Verbatim: "i have a full-on excel spreadsheet that i make every year for christmas um so i have my i i i'm being 1000 serious here um i have a i have a annual christmas excel sheet um which i use every single year um it has all my family on it it has it has my dog on it um it has any other family pets on it too and it has like um anytime i get an idea for a gift i'll put it on there and then yeah and then i keep track of like um getting good um wrapping and cards and like um making sure that like i don't overspend on one person so no one feels like left out and then yeah i have it with all the conditional formatting so then it comes up with the cool colors when i've done stuff or depending on how much is spent and things like that it's spreadsheets are fun okay no matter what anybody says spreadsheets are fun okay they are they are i i'm i'm tired of hiding it okay you can make some really fun things")
10. She enjoys using spreadsheets for organization and finds them fun. (Verbatim: "spreadsheets are fun okay no matter what anybody says spreadsheets are fun okay they are they are i i'm i'm tired of hiding it okay you can make some really fun things") [end of text]



1. She has a strong work ethic and takes responsibility for ensuring systems function properly despite difficult working conditions. (Verbatim: "i still felt like responsible for making sure things worked because it's not the customer's fault you know it's not the customer's fault")
2. She worked in a software-related role where she had to fix errors caused by colleagues who were intoxicated. (Verbatim: "basically clean up all their work for um for them making many mistakes while drunk to be honest")
3. She stayed sober during work to maintain responsibility and reliability. (Verbatim: "so i stayed sober so i could be the responsible one")
4. She has a history of working in a job she disliked due to underpayment and gender-based pay disparities. (Verbatim: "the fact that i was being underpaid and whatnot or the fact that they paid the guys more or something stupid")
5. She once had an ant infestation in her apartment despite living on a high floor, not the ground floor. (Verbatim: "i was on like third i think so i was pretty high up and there were all these ants in my flat")
6. She used poison-laced ant bait to eliminate an ant nest, which she felt guilty about afterward. (Verbatim: "the ants take the ant food and they take it back home and they you know it goes to all the ants to share all this food that they brought back and the food is poison")
7. She never dealt with a rodent problem in her university accommodation, which she now regrets. (Verbatim: "I never dealt with that but I feel like I should have dealt with that more importantly than the ants")
8. She has a large refrigerator but a small freezer, which she finds inconvenient. (Verbatim: "my fridge is actually really big it's my freezer that's really small like annoyingly small")
9. She uses a small stool to reach high shelves in both her fridge and wardrobe. (Verbatim: "i actually have a little stool that i do bring out um so what i do is i get my piano stool and i bring that over to the kitchen")
10. She enjoys the idea of raising an ant colony and sharing it with her audience as a shared project. (Verbatim: "i'd get an ant colony and i'd show you guys it and we could raise it together and it would be like our our ant baby") [end of text]



